  "operation": "Copy all methods of seven original upgrade/player-UI/red-dot/effect/use-item components. Preserve update order, next-level cost lookup, pending badge calculation branch, five player subscriptions, dirty red-dot update, property pool/background/effect order, success-only animation, use-item lifecycle, money-only shortage and merge-tip conditions. Adapt application parser/player/formula/typed-property/transaction calls to explicit consumed services; reuse original UIBase, ItemIcon, GameObjectPool and existing property presentation port.",
  "validated_scope": "Unity 2022.3.57f1c2 Direct3D Play Mode in an isolated project: exact original ProfessionPanel prefab and upgrade row, zero missing MonoBehaviours, original serialized upgrade references/state switcher/show clip and verified CN font config + full original Chinese binary text readers. Simulated mouse checks upgrade failure/deferred success and native use-item money-only shortage/fallthrough; source FIFO rows, zero omission, modulo-four backgrounds, previous/current/diff/cost order, changed-property effects and animation, badge/nonbadge/function/unlock/max red-dot branches, five player subscriptions, disable/re-enable/player-reinit cleanup passed. Native upgrade subtree screenshots were actually viewed at a matching 1080x1920 Game View/render target. Parent detail page initialization, character/level/name/tab data, typed property formatting, popup contents, player/formula/transactions, save and Windows publication are not validated and remain incomplete.",
